# {title}

Issued to all workers or employees (temporary or permanent) employed within the territorial jurisdiction of Calapan.

## Requirements

There are additional documents if you are a first-time job seeker.

### Documents

- Application Form (2 copies - secured from BPLO)
- Community Tax Certificate (Cedula)
- NBI Clearance or Police Clearance

### If first-time job seeker

- Barangay Certificate with an undertaking stating you are a first-time job seeker to avail the assistance.
- Medical Results (X-Ray Result)
- Urine and Stool test results (specifically required for food handlers)

## Step-by-step process

Follow these steps to claim your permit.

1. ### Secure application form

    Secure and fill out the application form at the Business Permit and Licensing Office (BPLO).

2. ### Submit requirements

    Submit the application form along with the required documents such as Cedula and NBI/Police Clearance for evaluation.

3. ### Assessment and payment

    Proceed through the assessment and pay the assessed fees as directed by the BPLO personnel.

4. ### Claim permit

    Claim the Occupational Permit once processed and approved.

